# Line endings: LF in every checkout, on every platform. The scripts run in WSL / bash (a CRLF `.sh` fails with "$'\r': command not found"),
# the generator signatures and the stored hashes are byte-exact (GtGenerator/.gitattributes says the same for its files), and a Windows git with
# core.autocrlf=true would otherwise turn every text file of a fresh clone into CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
# PowerShell 5.1 scripts: keep Windows line endings
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
